{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "At the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "No, Thanks!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > World of Food > Talking Around Food", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information involving apologies, thanks, suggestions and invitations in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Accepting and Refusing Invitations </span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you invite someone, you use the modals <span class=\"italic\">would</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span>. <br/> For example: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Would you like to come to dinner?</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You should come to my party!</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Could you come over later?</span><br/>You can also use the phrase <span class=\"italic\"> How about ... ?</span>  <br/><br/> It is important to respond in a polite way when a person invites you.<br/> You thank a person when you accept an invitation.<br/> You apologize when you refuse an invitation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Andrew:</span> How about eating pizza tonight? My treat!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Bobby:</span> Thanks! That's very kind of you!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Accepting an Invitation</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Refusing an Invitation</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">With pleasure!<br/>Thank you so much!<br/>That's very kind/sweet of you.<br/>Thank you for ...<br/>Great idea!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">Thanks, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">I would love to, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">I'm really sorry, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">Thank you for the offer, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">Sorry about that!</span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">Maybe next time!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jenna:</span> Would you like to watch an action movie?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Roy:</span> I would love to, but I need to work tonight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jessica:</span> You should come over for dinner later! <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Marie:</span> Great idea!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to veg out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend free time doing nothing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love to veg out in front of the TV!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you make plans with your friends.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "messy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not clean; not neat", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Chinese food is great but it's messy to eat in front of the TV.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I hope you don't mind", "type": "name"}, {"content": "I hope you are OK with it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: John and Sally are coming. I hope you don't mind!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "besides", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in addition; as well", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's invite John. Besides, I know you are good friends.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to keep someone company", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time with someone when they feel bored or lonely", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like all my friends to keep me company!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn3le01ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Think of something to do tonight. Write a dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Invite your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Respond to the invitation. Do you accept or refuse?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Accept? Use the right expressions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Refuse? Use the right expressions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange roles.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I accept and refuse invitations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write 30 to 50 words about plans for the evening.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use 3 target words about making plans.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn3le01ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn3le01ob10re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Would you like to get some food